WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
Take a moss shoot and a fern
frond, and leave both on a bench.

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:09.810
Suppose that after 20 minutes, the moss
is down to 49 per cent of its starting

3
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.750
mass.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.890
The fern is still at 95 per cent.

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.210
Both spread by spores.

6
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.220
Yet a fern lifts its
fronds into the light,

7
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.610
while a moss stays short.

8
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:26.740
So why can a fern stand tall,
while a moss stays low and damp?

9
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.220
In this mission, you'll take a moss apart,

10
00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.100
feature by feature.

11
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.810
Then you'll do the same for a fern, and
find the one weakness both plants still

12
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.070
share.

13
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: explain why a fern can stand
tall while a moss stays low and damp.
